  "body": "<p>Di’Trillio’s earlier work with the <a href=\"#cave-company\">Seekers</a> includes surviving the haze and investigating the harpy cave. His life with <a href=\"#vessalia\">Vessalia</a> gives his later risk a home to return to. The Dasa expedition turns technical investigation toward a political responsibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ditrillio-promise\">A promise carried beyond the embassy</h2>\n<p>Kimi and Kuri’s request leads him north from Pristinia with Saoirse, Felicity, Lucien, Alesteir and Vel’kaen. He checks the camp’s perimeter, helps organize watch and insists the company keep an attacker alive. After the surviving Rahu dies before explaining himself, Di’Trillio can establish only that the soldier did not kill himself; the cause remains unknown.</p><p class=\"source-note\">Scene references: <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1561173193048195203\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1561184576552833065\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1561220084217815074\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562280608682606685\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562282303793790997\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ditrillio-dignity\">Duty to the people on either side</h2>\n<p>He gives the fallen scouts shallow, respectful graves before pressing on. At the mountain refuge he approaches openly with his blades sheathed and bows to the siblings as equals. When Vey and Vaa distinguish their own purpose from an uprising, he corrects his assumption before offering more.</p><p class=\"source-note\">Scene references: <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562284518700753026\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562295072383438899\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562298018835992628\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562300016759021590\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ditrillio-bridge\">Becoming a bridge</h2>\n<p>He offers to seek Melian and the town elders’ support, help people who wish to leave and prepare a base for those who wish to resist. Eovar’s ships and a possible safehouse enter the discussion as practical needs. He accepts a sending stone and a night’s hospitality.</p><p>His pledge is witnessed. The town has not thereby approved his proposals, and the promised building, safehouse arrangements and departures are not shown complete.</p><p class=\"source-note\">Scene references: <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562302518992834604\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562303396306878485\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562304763209580648\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562305729417711618\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562308579396952168\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ditrillio-relationships\">People behind the work</h2>\n<p><a href=\"#vessalia\">Vessalia</a> is his partner; he tells Felicity they are enjoying their new home. <a href=\"#felicity\">Felicity</a> reminds him he has someone to return to. <a href=\"#saoirse\">Saoirse</a> adds offers of aid despite exhaustion. The <a href=\"#vey-vaa\">siblings</a> become contacts rather than merely names in someone else’s request.</p><p class=\"source-note\">Scene references: <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1561171920190312509\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1561198103258861660\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562302783229661298\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1562268792007164124/1562308140031148033\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ditrillio-work-at-home\">Service in the drains, care at home</h2>\n<p>Di’trillio trades weapons for cleaning tools in Pristinia’s square. Felicity joins him, and Vessalia helps with repeated cleaning magic. He encourages her contribution and treats Felicity as someone who has fought beside him, challenging the distance she places between servant and equal. Proposed deeper drains and a school still need other people’s agreement; cleaning has begun, not solved every civic problem.</p><p>At home he cooks a stew from his mother’s recipe, sharing the work and memories with Vessalia. Later, when the extended cleaning leaves her unwell, he carries her home. Their talk of marriage and children remains a shared hope. His explanations of his blood and concoctions are his account of his condition, rather than proof of a generally safe way to use Delerium.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ditrillio-dorothea\">An offered hand does not have to touch</h2><p>Di’trillio meets Dorothea Waldner at the Gate, visibly burned and frightened. When she stiffens at his approach, he stops. He sits down, leaves clean water within reach and offers a salve without requiring her to uncover herself for him. She refuses touch, and he respects that boundary.</p><p>Their conversation becomes easier when he shares that he lives with an injury he cannot simply cure. She recognizes something of her own suffering in it and eventually allows a visual examination. His offer of a quiet guest room remains subject to Vessalia’s agreement. He slows his walking to Dorothea’s pace as they leave. The scene offers care and consent rather than a miraculous cure.</p><h2 id=\"ditrillio-home-and-future\">Room for a guest, and a future imagined together</h2><p>Di’trillio asks Vessalia whether they can host Dorothea while she adjusts to Prima. Vessalia agrees and begins preparing a room, thinking about bedding that will not aggravate the burns. He wants her support while he learns to meet another injured person without hiding entirely behind his own mask.</p><p>They also talk about a wedding they might one day have. Vessalia wants a small gathering beneath the willow tree and refuses diamonds, explaining her revulsion at the labor she says her family uses to obtain them. Di listens and asks what she would prefer. No proposal, engagement ceremony or marriage occurs. The conversation ends with preparations for the guest and a shared walk to gather herbs.</p>",
