  "profile": {
    "personality": "An investigator whose promise to find two strangers becomes a commitment to help people choose between refuge and resistance.",
    "achievements": " Kimi and Kuri’s request leads him north from Pristinia with Saoirse, Felicity, Lucien, Alesteir and Vel’kaen. He checks the camp’s perimeter, helps organize watch and insists the company keep an attacker alive. After the surviving Rahu dies before explaining himself, Di’Trillio can establish only that the soldier did not kill himself; the cause remains unknown.   He gives the fallen scouts shallow, respectful graves before pressing on. At the mountain refuge he approaches openly with his blades sheathed and bows to the siblings as equals. When Vey and Vaa distinguish their own purpose from an uprising, he corrects his assumption before offering more. ",
    "relationships": "  Vessalia  is his partner; he tells Felicity they are enjoying their new home.  Felicity  reminds him he has someone to return to.  Saoirse  adds offers of aid despite exhaustion. The  siblings  become contacts rather than merely names in someone else’s request. "
  },
